WEBVTT

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Just like the cruel angel

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Young boy, become a legend

00:18.990 --> 00:22.410
2D4U PRESENTS:

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Aoi kaze ga ima

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Even though the untested breeze...

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
mune no doa o tataitemo

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
...taps at the door to your heart

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
You just look solely at me and smile

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
sono senaka ni wa

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
...that upon your back

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
You have the wings with which to fly...

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
no hane ga aru koto

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
...towards the distant future

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
The cruel angel's thesis

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
Omoide o uragiru nara

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
If you are to betray our memories

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Young boy, become a legend

01:31.570 --> 01:35.620
It seems you've refused to allow
the interrogation of the pilot of Unit 01,

01:35.620 --> 01:39.630
the only one directly involved
in the incident, Major Katsuragi.

01:39.630 --> 01:42.860
Yes, Sir. He is very unstable,
emotionally speaking.

01:42.860 --> 01:45.370
I believe that it would be
unwise to have him here.

01:45.370 --> 01:49.070
Then, as his proxy, let us ask you,
Major Katsuragi.

01:49.070 --> 01:50.470
In this incident,

01:50.470 --> 01:55.080
did the Angel not attempt to
communicate with us, mankind?

01:55.080 --> 01:57.810
I find no suggestion of that
in the subject's report.

01:57.810 --> 02:00.250
It is believed to have been an irregular incident.

02:00.250 --> 02:02.820
Assuming his memory is correct.

02:02.820 --> 02:05.490
There is no evidence that his memory
has been tampered with.

02:05.490 --> 02:08.590
However, the Eva's AC recorder
was not functioning.

02:08.590 --> 02:09.890
There's no way to confirm it.

02:09.890 --> 02:13.660
Was the Angel interested in the human psyche?
In the human mind?

02:13.660 --> 02:15.660
I am unable to answer that question.

02:15.660 --> 02:18.600
Whether the Angels even have
a concept of what a mind is,

02:18.600 --> 02:21.000
or whether they can understand
human thoughts or not,

02:21.000 --> 02:22.440
is completely unknown.

02:22.440 --> 02:28.040
This incident has a new element in it,
in that the Angel tried to take an Eva into itself.

02:28.040 --> 02:29.780
Is there any possibility that this

02:29.780 --> 02:33.650
may be linked to the predicted Thirteenth Angel
and all Angels thereafter?

02:33.650 --> 02:35.120
Based on the pattern thus far,

02:35.120 --> 02:38.190
there is nothing to suggest such a systematic
organization among the Angels.

02:38.190 --> 02:43.160
Correct! It is obvious that they have
worked independently, so far.

02:43.160 --> 02:45.030
What do you mean, Sir?

02:45.030 --> 02:47.060
You are not allowed to ask questions.

02:47.060 --> 02:47.560
Yes, Sir.

02:47.560 --> 02:49.460
That will be all. Dismissed.

02:49.460 --> 02:51.050
Yes, Sir.

02:52.410 --> 02:55.670
What do you think, Ikari?

02:55.670 --> 02:58.410
The Angels are beginning to attain intelligence.

02:58.410 --> 02:59.740
The time left to us is...

02:59.530 --> 03:02.660
EPISODE 17
THE FOURTH
QUALIFIED
INDIVIDUAL

02:59.740 --> 03:02.660
Running short?

03:05.560 --> 03:07.550
The patient in Room 12?

03:07.550 --> 03:09.680
The emergency room patient
from that E incident, right?

03:09.680 --> 03:11.920
She's been hospitalized here for a long time.

03:11.920 --> 03:14.590
I've heard her injuries are really complicated.

03:14.590 --> 03:16.460
She's still in elementary school.

03:16.460 --> 03:18.230
He's here again today, right?

03:18.230 --> 03:22.200
Yeah, he comes to see her
at least twice a week.

03:22.200 --> 03:24.630
He's a good and caring brother.

03:24.390 --> 03:29.890
Suzuhara

03:24.390 --> 03:29.890
Empty

03:24.390 --> 03:29.890
Empty

03:24.630 --> 03:28.890
Yeah, boys like that are pretty rare these days.

03:32.350 --> 03:34.510
Rei, are you all right today?

03:34.510 --> 03:38.180
Yes, Sir. I will go see Dr. Akagi tomorrow,

03:38.180 --> 03:40.420
and the day after I'll be at school.

03:40.420 --> 03:41.880
How is school?

03:41.880 --> 03:43.020
No problems, Sir.

03:43.020 --> 03:44.870
I see. That's good.

03:46.300 --> 03:49.410
Stand! Bow! Sit down!

03:51.510 --> 03:54.460
Today's absences are the usual Ayanami,
and Aida?

03:55.040 --> 03:57.200
What's up with Kensuke?

03:55.380 --> 03:58.700
Mr. Koike is also absent today,

03:57.200 --> 04:01.200
New Yokosuka. Chasin' battleships again today.

03:58.700 --> 04:01.970
So the class in modern Japanese
will be self-study.

04:01.200 --> 04:04.140
A ship called Myoko, or somethin'
like that, is in port.

04:01.970 --> 04:04.140
And finally, the student
on duty today will be...

04:04.140 --> 04:05.070
Suzuhara.

04:05.070 --> 04:06.810
Yes, Sir!

04:06.810 --> 04:09.740
Deliver the printouts to Ayanami after school.

04:09.740 --> 04:10.270
Yes, Sir!

04:13.690 --> 04:16.380
Anyway, 1st Branch is okay, right?

04:14.500 --> 04:17.420
Send the info from Satellite 5 immediately.
It's top priority.

04:15.030 --> 04:17.420
Just the schedule for Unit 04 is fine.

04:16.380 --> 04:20.400
It doesn't matter, we'll have the Magi evaluate
the data discrepancies from the sensors!

04:17.420 --> 04:20.400
I'd like confirmation on the synchro data
and the S2 engine.

04:17.420 --> 04:20.400
We'll get rid of the noise over on our end.
Just send us the originals.

04:20.900 --> 04:22.620
It vanished?!

04:22.620 --> 04:25.360
You're sure the 2nd Branch just vanished?!

04:25.360 --> 04:27.430
Yes, Sir, it's been confirmed.

04:27.430 --> 04:28.700
It vanished.

04:29.910 --> 04:31.300
Oh, man...

04:31.300 --> 04:33.870
The Administration and Investigation
departments are going crazy,

04:33.870 --> 04:35.800
and General Affairs is in a total panic.

04:35.800 --> 04:36.880
So what was the cause?

04:36.880 --> 04:38.470
We still don't know.

04:38.470 --> 04:41.240
Our only clues are these
geosynchronous satellite photos.

04:41.240 --> 04:43.420
There's nothing else left.

04:45.380 --> 04:47.030
10 seconds...

04:47.500 --> 04:48.620
8...

04:48.620 --> 04:49.550
7...

04:49.550 --> 04:50.520
6...

04:50.520 --> 04:51.420
5...

04:51.420 --> 04:52.350
4...

04:52.350 --> 04:53.190
3...

04:53.190 --> 04:54.060
2...

04:54.060 --> 04:54.940
1...

04:54.940 --> 04:56.480
Contact.

05:05.210 --> 05:06.670
This is horrible.

05:06.670 --> 05:11.670
Evangelion Unit 04 and all related
research facilities within an 89km radius

05:11.670 --> 05:13.210
have completely vanished.

05:13.210 --> 05:15.680
Along with several thousand people.

05:15.680 --> 05:19.010
Looking at the time schedule,
we believe it to be an accident

05:19.010 --> 05:22.220
during the experimental installation of
the S2 engine that was restored in Germany.

05:22.220 --> 05:23.520
Potential causes range from

05:23.520 --> 05:26.490
a lack of structural integrity to
a preliminary design stage error.

05:26.490 --> 05:29.220
That's 32,768 possibilities right there.

05:29.220 --> 05:31.330
And there's also the chance of sabotage.

05:31.330 --> 05:36.000
But it didn't explode, it vanished, right?
In other words, it disappeared.

05:36.000 --> 05:39.230
In all probability, they were swallowed
by a Sea of Dirac,

05:39.230 --> 05:40.870
just like Unit 01 was.

05:40.870 --> 05:43.140
And the S2 engine that we finally restored?

05:43.140 --> 05:45.510
Gone. Our dream's been shattered.

05:45.510 --> 05:48.510
That's what we get for trying to push ourselves
into using something we don't understand.

05:48.510 --> 05:50.450
That goes for the Evas too.

05:51.930 --> 05:54.580
So, what about the remaining Unit 03?

05:54.580 --> 05:56.750
We're going to base it here.

05:56.750 --> 06:00.090
It seems the U.S. Government doesn't
want to lose the 1st Branch as well.

06:00.090 --> 06:05.090
They're the ones who insisted on
the right to build Units 03 and 04.

06:05.090 --> 06:07.760
And now they're foisting just
the dangerous parts off on us?

06:07.760 --> 06:09.400
Talk about self-serving bastards.

06:09.400 --> 06:13.000
After a disaster like that,
anyone would get nervous.

06:13.000 --> 06:15.140
So what are you going to do
about the activation test?

06:15.140 --> 06:17.320
Will you use that dummy plug?

06:17.320 --> 06:18.520
I've still got to decide that.

06:21.060 --> 06:23.380
This is the dummy plug prototype.

06:23.380 --> 06:25.650
Rei's personal data has been loaded into it,

06:25.650 --> 06:29.650
but it's not really possible to digitize
a human mind and soul.

06:29.650 --> 06:32.420
Ultimately, it's a fake, an imitation.

06:32.420 --> 06:36.160
Just a machine that emulates
a pilot's thinking process.

06:36.160 --> 06:38.890
It'll transmit a signal pattern to the Eva.

06:38.890 --> 06:43.400
As long as the Eva believes there's a pilot
and synchronizes, that's enough.

06:43.400 --> 06:46.270
Load the data into Unit 01 and Unit 02.

06:46.270 --> 06:48.400
There are still some problems with it.

06:48.400 --> 06:51.070
That's not important. As long as
the Eva activates, it's sufficient.

06:51.070 --> 06:51.260
Yes, Sir.

06:54.420 --> 06:57.750
I've delegated the transportation
of the Unit to the U.N.

06:57.750 --> 07:00.050
It should arrive by the end of the week.

07:00.050 --> 07:02.120
You take care of the rest.

07:02.120 --> 07:03.180
Yes, Sir.

07:03.180 --> 07:06.650
We'll perform the modifications
and activation test in Matsushiro.

07:06.650 --> 07:08.060
What about the test pilot?

07:08.060 --> 07:10.060
The dummy plug is still risky.

07:10.060 --> 07:11.760
Of our prospective candidates...

07:11.760 --> 07:13.530
We'll select a fourth, then?

07:13.530 --> 07:18.200
Yes, there is one child whose core
can be prepared immediately.

07:18.200 --> 07:19.300
Then I'll leave it to you.

07:19.300 --> 07:20.890
Yes, Sir.

07:21.550 --> 07:23.760
Rei, you can come out now.

07:24.250 --> 07:25.510
Yes, Sir.

07:25.510 --> 07:26.940
Let's eat.

07:26.940 --> 07:27.960
Yes, Sir.

07:35.060 --> 07:37.310
Stand! Bow!

07:37.970 --> 07:42.590
Lunch time! Lunch time! This is the
single best thing 'bout school.

07:42.590 --> 07:44.510
What?!

07:45.670 --> 07:48.060
You didn't bring lunch?

07:48.060 --> 07:51.170
I didn't have time to cook last night
because of homework.

07:51.170 --> 07:55.310
And so you're telling me to go without lunch?!

07:55.850 --> 07:57.910
What's this? Married couple fightin' again?

08:02.720 --> 08:03.580
It's not like that!

08:05.390 --> 08:06.540
What's all this formality for?

08:07.830 --> 08:10.650
It's the Unit 03 activation test at Matsushiro.

08:10.650 --> 08:13.090
We'll be using the fourth as the pilot.

08:13.090 --> 08:14.290
The fourth?

08:14.290 --> 08:16.860
The Fourth Child's been found?

08:16.860 --> 08:18.360
Just yesterday.

08:18.360 --> 08:21.460
But I haven't received a report
from the Marduk Institute.

08:21.460 --> 08:23.440
The official documents will be
delivered tomorrow.

08:26.650 --> 08:30.710
Dr. Akagi, aren't you hiding
something from me again?

08:30.710 --> 08:32.170
Not really.

08:32.170 --> 08:35.630
Well, okay. So, who's the selected kid?

08:41.330 --> 08:43.990
Of all the people, it's that child?

08:43.990 --> 08:45.420
It can't be helped.

08:45.420 --> 08:47.960
All the candidates were gathered
together for protection.

08:47.960 --> 08:50.530
It'll be hard to break to them.

08:50.530 --> 08:54.330
Asuka will be fine. Her pride's
riding on her piloting of the Eva.

08:54.330 --> 08:56.730
And Rei is an exception,

08:56.730 --> 09:00.540
but nothing good comes of becoming
involved with us and the Evas.

09:00.540 --> 09:04.270
Shinji understands that better than anybody.

09:04.270 --> 09:07.220
I don't want him to suffer any more hardships.

09:07.220 --> 09:10.520
But we need children of this kind,

09:11.290 --> 09:13.920
in order for us all to survive.

09:13.920 --> 09:16.200
Let go of the pure ideals,
is that what you're saying?

09:24.770 --> 09:28.630
Suzuhara, you're on duty this week,
so get to it!

09:28.630 --> 09:29.700
What do you mean?

09:29.700 --> 09:31.530
The printout!

09:30.380 --> 09:31.460
Emergency Evacuation Training
Enforcement Notice

09:31.530 --> 09:34.100
Didn't our teacher tell you to deliver this?

09:34.100 --> 09:37.210
C'mon, class rep, you can ask
the other person on duty.

09:37.210 --> 09:39.340
Miss Ayanami is absent today!

09:39.340 --> 09:41.380
It's Ayanami and me?

09:41.380 --> 09:43.120
Can't be helped then.

09:43.560 --> 09:46.680
But I can't exactly go to a girl's place alone.

09:46.680 --> 09:48.320
Well, in that case, I'll go along...

09:48.320 --> 09:50.120
Shinji!

09:50.120 --> 09:51.060
Walk home with me, will ya?

10:14.990 --> 10:17.910
Ayanami, we're coming in.

10:17.910 --> 10:21.050
I don't think it's good to barge into
a girl's room without her permission.

10:21.050 --> 10:22.350
We've got no choice.

10:22.350 --> 10:23.890
She won't see it if we leave it there.

10:27.540 --> 10:28.770
Excuse us...

10:37.980 --> 10:39.830
Wha?!

10:39.830 --> 10:43.620
Is this a girl's room? It's so unwelcomin'.

10:51.420 --> 10:52.920
Notice
Class News

10:59.730 --> 11:02.720
Hey, you shouldn't touch anythin'!
She'll get pissed!

11:02.720 --> 11:04.810
I'm just cleaning up.

11:05.570 --> 11:07.800
I ain't helpin'!

11:07.800 --> 11:09.500
That's not a man's job!

11:09.500 --> 11:12.950
Okay, but Miss Misato hates guys like that.

11:14.780 --> 11:17.360
I don't care! It's my policy!

11:22.620 --> 11:25.260
Man, what a change.

11:25.930 --> 11:27.050
In what?

11:27.050 --> 11:27.910
You.

11:31.100 --> 11:35.300
The first time I saw you,
I really thought you were a jerk.

11:35.770 --> 11:38.880
And you didn't seem like you'd
do somethin' for others.

11:40.210 --> 11:43.880
Well, I guess it depends on
what you've got to give.

11:53.220 --> 11:54.840
We're visitin'!

11:54.840 --> 11:55.840
What?

11:55.840 --> 11:57.440
Those are the printouts that were pilin' up.

12:02.700 --> 12:04.450
I'm sorry.

12:04.450 --> 12:07.240
I took it upon myself to clean up a little.
But I didn't touch anything except trash.

12:10.370 --> 12:12.410
Thank you.

12:16.810 --> 12:21.630
Eva pilots sure are weird, all right.

12:29.820 --> 12:31.530
Thank you...

12:32.060 --> 12:34.420
Words of gratitude.

12:34.420 --> 12:35.690
Words I've never used.

12:38.870 --> 12:41.230
I'd never even said them to him.

12:48.610 --> 12:52.660
The city, a paradise made by mankind.

12:53.250 --> 12:55.600
Once driven from Paradise,

12:55.600 --> 12:59.720
man had no choice but to escape to this
earthly existence, side by side with death.

13:00.020 --> 13:02.110
Our own paradise,

13:02.110 --> 13:06.950
created by the resourcefulness that this
weakest of beings was forced to develop.

13:06.950 --> 13:09.550
To protect ourselves from the fear of death,

13:09.550 --> 13:12.320
to satiate our thirst for pleasure,

13:12.320 --> 13:15.140
a paradise we created ourselves.

13:15.970 --> 13:21.060
This city's truly such a paradise.
A armed city made to protect us.

13:21.060 --> 13:25.710
A city of cowards fleeing from
the outside world, filled with enemies.

13:27.280 --> 13:32.070
Cowards do live longer. That's fine.

13:32.070 --> 13:36.340
New Tokyo-3, Nerv's camouflaged
intercept fortress.

13:36.340 --> 13:40.050
The continually-delayed seventh
construction phase will be finished soon.

13:40.050 --> 13:42.420
At long last, it will be completed.

13:46.170 --> 13:50.970
How will you report Unit 04's accident
to the Committee?

13:50.970 --> 13:53.930
Just as the facts state, the cause is unknown.

13:54.440 --> 13:58.070
But at this stage, it's a catastrophic loss.

13:58.070 --> 14:00.300
Unit 04 and the 2nd Branch are acceptable.

14:00.300 --> 14:02.840
Even with the S2 engine,
we may have lost the sample,

14:02.840 --> 14:05.470
but we still have the data in Germany.

14:05.470 --> 14:08.380
This installation and Unit 01 will be sufficient.

14:08.380 --> 14:11.160
But the Committee was furious.

14:11.630 --> 14:14.260
Of course, it was an unscheduled accident.

14:14.260 --> 14:17.710
Seele must also be frantically
adjusting the schedule.

14:18.430 --> 14:21.120
Incidents not depicted in the
Dead Sea Scrolls can occur.

14:21.120 --> 14:23.600
This ought to teach the old men a lesson.

14:28.230 --> 14:31.130
The intercept system here is finally
going to be completed,

14:31.130 --> 14:33.970
and there isn't even one measly party planned?

14:33.970 --> 14:36.000
Nerv sure is an uptight organization.

14:36.000 --> 14:37.890
Well, you know how Commander Ikari is.

14:38.550 --> 14:40.230
What about you?

14:40.690 --> 14:42.710
Are you serious, Mr. Kaji?

14:42.710 --> 14:45.750
I'll tell Miss Katsuragi and Dr. Akagi.

14:45.750 --> 14:47.850
I'll cover up your mouth first...

14:47.850 --> 14:49.580
So how's work going?

14:49.580 --> 14:51.590
Oh, it's going, I guess.

14:51.590 --> 14:54.400
Well, I have work to do. Excuse me.

14:55.470 --> 14:58.800
Far be it from me to comment
on your private life,

15:00.240 --> 15:03.460
but would you keep your hands off
our young girls in this emergency situation?

15:03.460 --> 15:05.730
This isn't your jurisdiction, though, is it?

15:05.730 --> 15:07.500
Could I hit on you then?

15:07.500 --> 15:09.300
That depends on how you answer my questions.

15:09.300 --> 15:12.430
You know the secrets of Adam down there
and the Marduk Institute, right?

15:13.510 --> 15:14.680
What secrets?

15:14.680 --> 15:16.240
Don't play dumb!

15:16.240 --> 15:18.780
Asking for help isn't like you.

15:18.780 --> 15:22.350
I can't afford to care right now.
I don't have that luxury.

15:22.350 --> 15:26.350
What's behind the oh-so-convenient
discovery of the Fourth Child?

15:26.350 --> 15:28.910
I'll tell you one thing.

15:30.470 --> 15:32.460
The Marduk Institute doesn't exist.

15:32.460 --> 15:35.130
Nerv itself is pulling the strings.

15:35.130 --> 15:36.930
Nerv itself?

15:36.930 --> 15:37.830
Commander Ikari?

15:37.830 --> 15:40.300
Go check out Code 707.

15:40.300 --> 15:41.890
707?

15:42.650 --> 15:44.440
Shinji's school?

15:44.440 --> 15:46.170
Miss Misato!

15:46.170 --> 15:46.970
What is it?

15:46.970 --> 15:50.110
Miss Ritsuko wants to see you about
the business trip you're going on tomorrow.

15:50.110 --> 15:51.010
All right. Thank you.

15:52.090 --> 15:53.310
I'll catch you later.

15:53.310 --> 15:54.140
Yes, Ma'am.

15:58.030 --> 16:00.690
How about it? Wanna go out for tea?

16:00.690 --> 16:02.100
You know, I'm a boy.

16:06.900 --> 16:10.840
I thought you'd be a more
serious person, Mr. Kaji.

16:11.180 --> 16:14.500
Once you're comfortable around someone,
you sure don't hold back, Shinji Ikari.

16:14.500 --> 16:16.800
I'm sorry.

16:16.800 --> 16:20.450
No, I'm sorry too. I didn't mean
to sound sarcastic.

16:21.890 --> 16:25.260
I know! I'll show you something neat.

16:27.700 --> 16:30.180
Are they watermelons?

16:30.180 --> 16:33.070
Yeah, aren't they cute? This is my hobby.

16:33.670 --> 16:34.970
It's a secret from everybody else, though.

16:36.040 --> 16:39.160
Making something...
Nurturing something is really great.

16:39.160 --> 16:40.850
You can see and learn so many things
from the process.

16:41.840 --> 16:43.830
Like what's enjoyable.

16:43.830 --> 16:45.420
And about suffering too, right?

16:48.480 --> 16:50.190
Do you hate suffering?

16:50.750 --> 16:52.440
I don't like it.

16:52.440 --> 16:53.700
Have you found anything that you enjoy?

16:57.260 --> 16:58.750
That's fine too.

16:58.750 --> 17:03.380
But knowledge of suffering makes you
all the more capable of kindness to others.

17:03.380 --> 17:05.370
Because that's different from being weak.

17:06.770 --> 17:08.470
Yes? Hello?

17:10.870 --> 17:12.460
It's Katsuragi.

17:12.460 --> 17:14.420
She says they're starting the synch test.

17:14.740 --> 17:17.340
<i>Fix the depth at 3.2.</i>

17:16.240 --> 17:20.530
I thought so. Shinji's synch rate is dropping.

17:17.340 --> 17:19.470
<i>LCL thickness is nominal.</i>

17:19.470 --> 17:22.640
<i>Harmonics level is negative 1.1...</i>

17:20.530 --> 17:21.940
What's that mean?

17:21.940 --> 17:23.500
I can't say.

17:22.640 --> 17:23.670
<i>0.5...</i>

17:23.500 --> 17:26.840
But something must have happened
during that incident.

17:23.670 --> 17:24.970
<i>0.9...</i>

17:24.970 --> 17:27.680
<i>0.10...</i>

17:26.840 --> 17:28.710
Something psychological.

17:27.680 --> 17:30.010
<i>Current exponent is 0.9.</i>

17:28.710 --> 17:31.880
This makes it even harder to tell him
about Unit 03's pilot.

17:30.010 --> 17:33.900
<i>All results posted to Melchior.</i>

17:31.880 --> 17:35.110
But the pilot will be officially informed tomorrow.

17:38.470 --> 17:41.610
Stand! Attention! Bow!

17:42.240 --> 17:44.760
Lunch time!

17:42.240 --> 17:44.760
<i><i>Toji Suzuhara of Class 2-A.</i></i>

17:44.760 --> 17:47.500
<i><i>Toji Suzuhara, report to the Principal's Office.</i></i>

17:47.500 --> 17:48.960
What the...

17:48.960 --> 17:50.550
Did you do something?

17:51.250 --> 17:53.750
No, nothin' comes to mind.

17:54.130 --> 18:02.180
Principal's Office

17:56.180 --> 17:58.460
Excuse me, I'm Toji Suzuhara.

18:00.120 --> 18:02.140
You're Toji Suzuhara?

18:04.690 --> 18:07.010
How was your trip to New Yokosuka yesterday?

18:07.010 --> 18:08.380
Way cool!

18:08.380 --> 18:11.560
Speaking of which, I picked up
some interesting information.

18:13.100 --> 18:14.890
Eva Unit 03?

18:14.890 --> 18:18.930
Yeah, the one they were building in America.
It's completed, isn't it?

18:18.930 --> 18:20.390
I don't know.

18:20.390 --> 18:24.030
I know you've got to keep it a secret,
but please tell me.

18:24.030 --> 18:25.900
I really haven't heard anything!

18:25.900 --> 18:27.770
Haven't you heard the rumor
that the activation test

18:27.770 --> 18:30.240
will be held at the second test facility
in Matsushiro?

18:30.240 --> 18:31.270
I haven't.

18:31.270 --> 18:33.210
The pilot hasn't been chosen yet, right?

18:33.210 --> 18:35.060
I don't know about that stuff.

18:35.460 --> 18:38.980
I wish Miss Misato would pick me for it.

18:38.980 --> 18:42.780
Hey, Shinji, would you ask her for me too?
I want to be an Eva pilot!

18:42.780 --> 18:44.140
Really, I don't know.

18:46.200 --> 18:49.960
Then what about the story
that Unit 04's been lost?

18:49.960 --> 18:50.990
What was that?

18:50.990 --> 18:52.770
You really don't know about that either?

18:53.570 --> 18:55.900
It disappeared along with the entire 2nd Branch.

18:55.900 --> 18:58.300
I heard my dad's section was in a panic.

18:58.300 --> 18:59.430
Really?

18:59.430 --> 19:00.940
Probably.

19:00.940 --> 19:02.780
I haven't heard anything from Miss Misato.

19:04.590 --> 19:08.080
Well, I guess it doesn't concern
pilots out on the line.

19:08.080 --> 19:11.710
If she didn't tell you, it's likely because
you don't need to know.

19:13.130 --> 19:16.100
Sorry about bothering you with weird questions.

19:17.260 --> 19:20.560
But Toji sure is taking a long time.

19:20.970 --> 19:22.660
Thus, we, mankind,

19:22.660 --> 19:27.600
survived the hell on Earth called
the Second Impact and rose again.

19:27.600 --> 19:30.100
The number of children has
been decreasing yearly...

19:30.100 --> 19:32.200
Sorry I'm late.

19:32.200 --> 19:34.870
I've already heard. Take your seat.

19:34.870 --> 19:38.320
Anyway, it is you, the younger generation,
who will lead the way to the future...

19:41.820 --> 19:43.780
Come on, let's go home.

19:43.780 --> 19:44.710
What about Toji?

19:44.710 --> 19:46.810
He'll be late.

19:46.810 --> 19:48.450
He's got class duty.

19:58.410 --> 20:00.090
The school is now closing.

20:00.090 --> 20:03.420
All students must go home immediately.

20:01.710 --> 20:03.420
Suzuhara!

20:04.150 --> 20:06.950
You're on duty,

20:07.550 --> 20:10.600
so make sure you line up the desks
and write up the daily record.

20:10.600 --> 20:14.780
I haven't had lunch yet.
I'll do it as soon as I've eaten.

20:14.780 --> 20:17.650
Suzuhara, you always buy your lunch
from the school co-op.

20:17.650 --> 20:19.360
It's not like I've got anyone to cook for me.

20:22.660 --> 20:24.110
Suzuhara...

20:24.110 --> 20:24.860
Milk

20:25.730 --> 20:30.060
I have two sisters, named Kodama and Nozomi.

20:30.060 --> 20:32.610
I always cook lunch for them, but...

20:32.910 --> 20:34.830
Must be a lot of work.

20:34.830 --> 20:39.030
So, I'm actually a good cook,
though you might not think it.

20:39.030 --> 20:40.530
Really?

20:40.530 --> 20:44.450
And I always end up cooking
too much for our lunches.

20:44.750 --> 20:47.050
What a waste.

20:47.460 --> 20:50.340
If you need help gettin' rid
of your leftovers, I'll help.

20:50.340 --> 20:52.890
Yes, help me.

20:52.890 --> 21:00.690
District 3 transformation test complete.

21:00.690 --> 21:01.660
Mr. Kaji?

21:01.660 --> 21:05.070
Oh, Asuka? Sorry, I'm a little busy
right now. Later, okay?

21:07.140 --> 21:09.180
But you make time for Misato.

21:13.050 --> 21:15.480
Hey, not right now!

21:16.020 --> 21:18.590
These are our synch data reports, right?

21:19.050 --> 21:20.670
Four of them?

21:20.670 --> 21:23.360
What in the hell is this? What's going on?

21:23.360 --> 21:25.910
Why is HE the Fourth Child?

21:25.910 --> 21:28.890
No! I don't understand! What is this?!

21:28.930 --> 21:31.640
NERV 1st BRANCH, USA

21:57.920 --> 22:00.710
TO BE CONTINUED

23:06.230 --> 23:07.240
PREVIEW

23:07.190 --> 23:12.290
Eva Unit 03 is delivered to Matsushiro
from America for the activation test.

23:12.290 --> 23:17.400
Unaware of the coming tragedy,
people gloried in the last of their daily lives.

23:17.400 --> 23:20.010
Next episode: "The Selection of Life"

23:19.080 --> 23:21.250
THE SELECTION OF LIFE
